  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Mary Lazare described a prize competition aimed at identifying technologies that empower caregivers, reduce caregiver burnout, and expand access to high-quality care at home. She said the Administration for Community Living was beginning to look at AI in wearables and home modifications to help people remain in their homes. In June 2026 remarks, she outlined using AI to support caregivers, target employment and accommodations for people with disabilities, connect people to economic-security resources, and match callers to resources.",
   "sids": [
    "s2",
